PROC arlaunch:
rem This little piece of OPL will let you
rem launch a program with a dynamically
rem generated filename (which requires
rem something more elaborate that AuroRun's
rem built in macroes.  Good if you want
rem to edit a different timesheet, or
rem something, each week.

rem This uses a trick with macsys to execute
rem the required program, but there's no
rem reason why you couldn't invoke it
rem directly with an OS call.

rem Unless the AutoRun definition has the
rem same "name" as the program invoked by
rem this OPL, it will launch it every time
rem the configuration file is processed.  In
rem this case, its therefore appropriate to
rem use the 'once' condition in the when
rem field.

global prog$(8),file$(128),ppppid%,wk%,wk$(2)

prog$="Sheet"
wk%=week(day,month,year)-40
if wk%<0 :wk%=wk%+53 :endif
wk$=right$("0"+gen$(wk%,2),2)
file$="m:\spr\time"+right$(gen$(year,4),2)+wk$+".spr"

loadm "m:\app\macro.opa"
runappb:(prog$,file$)
unloadm "m:\app\macro.opa"
ENDP
